+# TASK-260715-39xz9g — tester rework handoff
+
+## Outcome
+
+The reviewed fixture gap is closed by an executable, candidate-neutral
+orchestration path in `scripts/ssh_matrix_fixture.py` and its task-scoped public
+contract `TASK-260715-39xz9g_ssh-matrix-orchestration-v1.md`.
+
+The runner resolves each manifest server through an external command reference;
+requires prepare, rotation disposition, least-privilege probe, and zero-residual
+teardown; starts the direct-tcpip destinations on the SSH server; supplies
+long-lived stdio echo/sink commands; puts latency and deterministic loss proxies
+on the effective SSH TCP path; and requires identical complete scenario coverage
+from the libssh2 and ReluxNIOSSH driver IDs. Success is required against current
+macOS, current Linux, the approved fallback profile, and the real relux row.
+Negative host/auth cases remain confined to task-owned fixtures.
+
+Runtime host, port, user, and identity data remain in process memory. Reports
+admit only categorical OS/OpenSSH facts, public fingerprints and key types,
+candidate/server/scenario IDs, public observation codes, rotation disposition,
+and teardown status. Provider and driver failures redact stdout/stderr.
+
+The ReluxNIOSSH adapter task is currently blocked and the two real functional
+matrix tasks remain backlog. This task therefore validates the complete fixture
+and driver contract with controlled drivers; it does not claim a real
+dual-candidate selection result. Those later tasks can run the checked-in
+`orchestrate` command without changing the fixture matrix.
+
+## Validation evidence
+
+- `make ssh-fixtures-test`: exit 0; 28 tests passed.
+- Python stdlib `trace --missing --summary`: exit 0; 83.5% line coverage for
+  `scripts/ssh_matrix_fixture.py`.
+- `swift test --filter LibSSH2AdapterIntegrationTests`: exit 0; 26 tests passed.
+- `swift test`: exit 0; 428 tests in 35 suites passed.
+- Python compilation, manifest JSON parsing, strict Swift format lint, and
+  `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+- Approved `ssh-config://relux` categorical probe: exit 0; non-root, Darwin,
+  OpenSSH 9.9p2. No host, address, user, key path, or remote content was emitted.
+- Existing full 5 GiB stream evidence remains exact at 5,368,709,120 bytes and
+  `SHA256:fc01cfd7aebf90ff9491f8556131b6ef575c3e1fa33a0277ba28920bbaee7f54`,
+  with no retained payload.
+
+## Teardown evidence
+
+Tests prove reverse-order provider teardown after candidate failure and require
+`residualResources: 0`. Endpoint listeners and impairment proxy sockets are
+closed on all tested paths. The prior real fixture run removed the task Lima VM,
+ephemeral keys, hashed known-hosts state, raw diagnostics, and payload scratch.
+The real-host identity remains externally owner-managed and is never rotated or
+stored by this repository.
