    35	The orchestrator requires both candidate IDs to observe every scenario. The
    36	success scenario runs against all four server rows. Destructive negative cases
    37	use only task-owned macOS fixtures; they never change the real relux host. The
    38	latency and loss rows receive a numeric-loopback TCP proxy as their SSH endpoint,
    39	so impairment is applied to the connection actually exercised by the driver.
    40	
    41	## Provider protocol
    42	
    43	The orchestrator invokes each provider command with one canonical JSON object
    44	on stdin and expects one JSON object on stdout. Stderr is always redacted on
    45	failure.
    46	
    47	The request protocol is `relux-ssh-matrix-provider-v1`. Actions are:
    48	
    49	- `prepare`: provision a task-owned server or resolve an owner-managed one,
    50	  start the six task-owned destination listeners on that SSH server, and make
    51	  the stdio commands available; return `status: ok` and an in-memory `runtime`
    52	  containing `host`, `port`, `identityReference`, and the complete numeric-IPv4
    53	  `destinationEndpoints` map.
    54	- `rotate`: rotate a task-owned fixture credential, or report
    55	  `external-owner-managed` for the approved real-host identity; return
    56	  `status: ok`, `disposition`, and optionally a replacement `runtime`.
    57	- `probe`: prove non-root reachability after rotation. Return `status: ok` and
    58	  exactly the public observation fields accepted by the orchestrator:
    59	  `architecture`, `hostKeyFingerprints`, `opensshVersion`, `osName`,
    60	  `osVersion`, `privilege`, `reachable`, and `userKeyTypes`.
    61	- `teardown`: remove only task-owned processes, listeners, VM state, ephemeral
    62	  credentials, and known-hosts state. Return `status: ok` and
    63	  `residualResources: 0`.
    64	
    65	Providers resolve the manifest's `ephemeral-memory://`, `lima-store://`, and
    66	`ssh-config://` references. Runtime descriptors may contain sensitive routing
    67	and identity data because they travel only in process memory. They are never
    68	copied into the matrix report.
    69	
    70	## Candidate-driver protocol
    71	
    72	Each driver receives protocol `relux-ssh-matrix-driver-v1` with the candidate,
    73	server, and scenario IDs, the in-memory server runtime, the effective SSH
    74	endpoint, all direct-tcpip destination addresses, the selected network profile,
    75	and these public long-lived exec commands:
    76	
    77	```text
    78	python3 -u scripts/ssh_matrix_fixture.py stdio-echo
    79	python3 -u scripts/ssh_matrix_fixture.py stdio-sink
    80	```
    81	
    82	Providers launch each direct-tcpip destination with
    83	`python3 -u scripts/ssh_matrix_fixture.py serve-endpoint --mode <mode>` and
    84	read its first stdout line for the numeric-loopback address. The modes are
    85	`echo`, `sink`, `early-close`, `half-close`, `reset`, and `disconnect`.
    86	
    87	The driver returns only `status: pass`, the matching `scenarioId`, and a public
    88	`observationCode` prefixed by `<scenarioId>:`. A declaration, skipped row,
    89	missing candidate, or malformed result fails closed and prevents report
    90	creation.
    91	
    92	## Teardown and privacy
    93	
    94	Provider teardown runs in reverse preparation order even when provisioning,
    95	probing, or a candidate row fails. The endpoint set and all impairment proxies
    96	are task-owned numeric-loopback listeners and are stopped on every path. A
    97	successful report records public observations, matrix outcomes, rotation
    98	dispositions, zero-residual teardown evidence, and `payloadRetention: none`.
    99	It excludes every runtime descriptor and is scanned for private-key and
   100	password markers before output.
   101	
   102	Credential rotation for the real relux identity remains owner-managed: this
   103	fixture proves the external reference and least-privilege access but does not
   104	mutate a non-task-owned account. Task-owned macOS/Linux providers must return
   105	`rotated` after replacing their ephemeral identity.

